# Gate step 1650-fb7z — the preflight door removes a stale .git/index.lock that
# a guard's git left, and only such a lock. A git SIGKILLed while it holds the
# lock (proc.run's timeout_ms KILLs the group; the Lua guard then ends on its
# own) runs no cleanup. build.sh's _pf_run_guard and _pf_sweep_late are
# extracted against a scratch git repository: the trunk door (both sweep calls
# removed) leaves the lock, the fixed door removes it and names it, and a lock
# a live process holds, or one older than the run, is never removed.
#
# STEP_LUA is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking the door sweeps a stale index.lock a killed git left, and never a held one (1650-fb7z)"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/test-door-index-lock-sweep.lua"
STEP_ERROR="the preflight door no longer removes a stale index.lock a killed git left, or removed one a live process holds or one older than the run (1650-fb7z) — see the FAIL lines above"
STEP_OK="Door index-lock sweep fixture passed"
# 1765-q7rg: the sweep races a killed git under host load, so one red is
# retried once after a settle and a second reads flaky:.
STEP_HOST_STATE="load"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="yolanda-windows 2026-10-13 msys ok:door-index-lock-sweep:8 arms"
# ORDER 2155-gpar: runs alone, never beside a sibling step in the gate pool.
STEP_SERIAL="reads host state"
STEP_LANES="host"
# ORDER 2157-ginp: STEP_READS, the paths this step reads, RECORDED ONLY: never
# consulted by the class-selector skip (that is STEP_INPUTS, 2118-tnut). First
# cut: the step's own script plus every repo path it names literally.
STEP_READS="scripts/lua/test-door-index-lock-sweep.lua"
# ORDER 2177-dils (priority:build-speed): STEP_INPUTS, the class selector may skip
# this step when no changed path intersects them (2118-tnut). The fixture does
# NOT run the door: it extracts the _pf_* sweep functions from build.sh (an
# implicit input) and runs them in scratch repos, so its closure is nameable.
# Static: the extracted functions name no script. Atime trace of a real run
# (calmecacpilli 2026-11-22): build.sh, this fixture, .tillandsias/*.yaml (the
# plan binary's command policy) and nothing else.
# path:.gitignore: the Lua runtime reads it on every script run (lenovinha's
# trace, 2026-11-22), so it is declared too. The Lua guard it plants runs
# on the plan binary, hence rust. Door-level coverage stays in 885-1753-p925,
# which declares no inputs and always runs.
STEP_INPUTS="rust path:.tillandsias/* path:.gitignore"
